Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Settings menu: show controller focus, LB/RB switch tabs

Driving Settings > Controls with the D-pad moved focus down the key bindings
but nothing lit up (bindDefs and buttons only highlight under the mouse), so
input looked lost. Reaching another tab meant walking every row.

- While a controller drives a classic menu, the desktop outlines its focused
  control after drawing (idWindow::DrawControllerFocus), clipped to scrolled
  lists and only when every ancestor is visible.
- LB/RB press the previous/next Settings tab button (Controls, Game Options,
  Display, Audio) through the new idUserInterface::RunWindowAction, then focus
  the new page's first control. Page scrolling moves to LT/RT, which also take
  over the held-key repeat.
- gui_debugControllerFocus 1 prints each focus move.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
